{"version":1,"content":"<html>\n<body>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/CW_2807-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<p>Two days ago (the 10th), the Home Affairs Department announced the \"Woh Tsai Shan Improvement Plan\", which will phase out illegal structures that have long been placed on Bishop's Hill in Sham Shui Po. The first phase covers the area from the foothill to the summit of the Tong Yam Street hillside rest area, while the second phase covers the foothill to the summit near Berwick Street.</p>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/CW_2834-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<p>Currently, the second phase area still retains a number of fitness equipment and deity statues, with residents seen kicking shuttlecocks, playing table tennis, and using fitness equipment on site. As for the area around the Tong Yam Street hillside rest area, barbed wire and hoardings were already put up last night, with security guards stationed there this morning to prohibit residents from entering.</p>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/CW_3017-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/CW_2999-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/CW_2938-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/CW_2637-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/CW_2292-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/CW_2304-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/CW_2303-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/CW_2572-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/CW_2651-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/CW_2567-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/CW_2671-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/CW_2667-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/CW_2495-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/CW_2508-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/CW_2465-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Payme-500x237.png\"/>\n</body>\n</html>","scraped_at":"2026-08-13T09:26:55.588277+00:00","quality":{"score":1,"chars":169,"images":18,"source":"The Collective HK","fallback":"none"}}